{"id": "EUVD-2026-101065", "enisaUuid": "dd23e5e4-8b5a-39db-8070-3ce1bbee7acb", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndmaengine: ti: k3-udma-glue: fix NULL dereference in k3_udma_glue_release_rx_chn()\n\nIf devm_kcalloc() for rx_chn->flows fails in a channel request function,\nthe error path calls k3_udma_glue_release_rx_chn(), which dereferences\nthe NULL rx_chn->flows pointer in k3_udma_glue_release_rx_flow().\n\nSkip the flow release loop in k3_udma_glue_release_rx_chn() when\nrx_chn->flows is not allocated.\n\nFound by Linux Verification Center (linuxtesting.org) with SVACE.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T13:27:47", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:19:10", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b51ed7885ab0e8ecad765adc13b465cb1498cdc9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b2985956e06632939bee47cee13bccd78ad7c3a1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/967612574c542dec71f820a6eb16dea80dd187a1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/89f5414660724bb562db4ac74665da16d4a57d99", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5a6cb4d387eebf7d32a6ed3fcd39f94bf38bd134", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b14e6c52872556de2d6c137531e0ce85085c10ed", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5b2d92b7b177226e1dca2e80dc8369131276c2a4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0294b6dd515256c03ea2dbf508ddd3826d788579"], "aliases": ["GHSA-g7ff-rm89-vv7r", "CVE-2026-98416"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.22, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0e13927f-245e-3bd0-934b-e9e8195c4da7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d702419134133db1eab2067dc6ea5723467fd917 <b51ed7885ab0e8ecad765adc13b465cb1498cdc9"}, {"id": "12f521b1-f4ba-387d-bbdd-c0003d80dc60", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d702419134133db1eab2067dc6ea5723467fd917 <0294b6dd515256c03ea2dbf508ddd3826d788579"}, {"id": "17c9c35a-eda6-3794-9a21-1fe9fd1c2fdc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "prod